  "title": "Shopping",
  "description": "Learn how to ask for prices, navigate stores, and buy items in Korean.",
  "guidebook": "### Essential Shopping Phrases\n\nWhen shopping in Korea, asking for prices is simple! Just point and ask:\n* **이거 얼마예요?** (*Igeo eolmayeyo?*) — \"How much is this?\"\n\n### Payment Methods with -(으)로\nTo indicate your payment method, attach the particle **-(으)로** (\"by\" or \"with\"):\n* **카드로** (*kadeuro*) — \"by card\"\n* **현금으로** (*hyeongeum-euro*) — \"with cash\"\nPair it with **계산해 주세요** (*gyesanhae juseyo*, \"please charge/check out\").\n\n### Cheap vs. Expensive\n* **비싸요** (*bissayo*) = \"It is expensive.\"\n* **싸요** (*ssayo*) = \"It is cheap.\"\n\nAdd **너무** (*neomu*, \"too\") when something exceeds your budget: **너무 비싸요** (*neomu bissayo*, \"It's too expensive!\").",
